- Are we ready?
- I'm set.

1256
00:41:30,238 --> 00:41:31,238
Let's go.

1257
00:41:31,238 --> 00:41:32,408
- Good luck.
- In 1, 2, 3.

1258
00:41:32,408 --> 00:41:33,478
- Go!
- Go!

1259
00:41:33,478 --> 00:41:34,908
(Good luck on the last try.)

1260
00:41:37,078 --> 00:41:38,178
- Here we go.
- Please.

1261
00:41:38,178 --> 00:41:39,848
- Here we go.
- You're ready, right?

1262
00:41:40,318 --> 00:41:42,218
Ready. Set.

1263
00:41:42,218 --> 00:41:44,818
(Out of 10 total tries, they're on the last try.)

1264
00:41:44,838 --> 00:41:51,848
(Last try, John Park)

1265
00:41:51,848 --> 00:41:53,918
(Last try, Jae Seok)

1266
00:41:53,918 --> 00:41:55,748
- Please.
- You can do it.

1267
00:41:58,018 --> 00:41:59,688
You can do it.

1268
00:42:03,770 --> 00:42:06,140
(It's the 3rd player, Woo Jae's turn.)

1269
00:42:06,140 --> 00:42:09,570
(Last try, Woo Jae)

1270
00:42:11,473 --> 00:42:13,673
(Even Woo Jae succeeded!)

1271
00:42:15,203 --> 00:42:17,443
(Last try, Yeon Seok)

1272
00:42:17,443 --> 00:42:19,943
(It's a success if Yeon Seok makes the box stand.)

1273
00:42:25,213 --> 00:42:27,683
Yeon Seok, you've always done it.

1274
00:42:28,483 --> 00:42:30,923
You're Yoo One Shot. You always succeed.

1275
00:42:34,663 --> 00:42:37,063
(The last try)

1276
00:42:37,063 --> 00:42:38,433
Don't shake it.

1277
00:42:38,433 --> 00:42:41,403
(And the last player)

1278
00:42:46,333 --> 00:42:47,443
Success!

1279
00:42:47,443 --> 00:42:49,803
(They've succeeded in the mission.)

1280
00:42:52,143 --> 00:42:53,143
Success!

1281
00:42:53,143 --> 00:42:55,283
(Yeon Seok did it.)

1282
00:42:56,683 --> 00:42:59,853
(They finally succeeded on the last try.)

1283
00:43:01,583 --> 00:43:04,553
(A miracle made by four people)

1284
00:43:08,993 --> 00:43:09,993
Thank you!

1285
00:43:10,163 --> 00:43:11,833
- Success!
- Nice!

1286
00:43:11,833 --> 00:43:12,833
Success!

1287
00:43:13,093 --> 00:43:15,303
And in the last minute. Amazing.

1288
00:43:15,303 --> 00:43:16,533
Look at Woo Jae.

1289
00:43:16,863 --> 00:43:18,173
(The Whenever Friends have passed out.)

1290
00:43:18,173 --> 00:43:19,173
Are you praying?

1291
00:43:19,173 --> 00:43:20,373
Earlier...

1292
00:43:20,373 --> 00:43:23,173
Earlier, he was skeptical about the joy we felt.

1293
00:43:23,673 --> 00:43:24,813
He was skeptical about how happy we get.

1294
00:43:24,813 --> 00:43:27,213
- Yeon Seok, thank you so much.
- What are you...

1295
00:43:27,343 --> 00:43:28,413
Really.

1296
00:43:28,413 --> 00:43:29,783
Thank you so much.

1297
00:43:30,143 --> 00:43:31,253
Round Three,

1298
00:43:31,253 --> 00:43:33,483
- success!
- Success!

1299
00:43:33,483 --> 00:43:34,983
(Succeeded Round 3 on the 10th try)

1300
00:43:37,293 --> 00:43:39,553
(Yoo One Shot lived up to his name.)

1301
00:43:39,893 --> 00:43:40,893
You feel drained, right?

1302
00:43:40,893 --> 00:43:42,623
(John or Park is exhausted.)

1303
00:43:42,623 --> 00:43:44,493
John or Park did a great job.

1304
00:43:44,863 --> 00:43:46,063
He was reliable.

1305
00:43:46,063 --> 00:43:48,263
- But really...
- How was it?

1306
00:43:49,333 --> 00:43:50,333
Gosh.

1307
00:43:50,463 --> 00:43:52,303
("I don't think I'll be that happy even if we succeed today.")

1308
00:43:52,303 --> 00:43:54,143
(By Joo Woo Jae 1 hour ago)

1309
00:43:54,143 --> 00:43:55,743
You didn't know why we got all happy.

1310
00:43:55,743 --> 00:43:57,473
To be frank, had we failed right now,

1311
00:43:57,913 --> 00:43:59,313
the guilt would've lasted for two months.

1312
00:44:00,443 --> 00:44:01,583
(Woo Jae has been saved.)

1313
00:44:01,583 --> 00:44:02,883
Really, I... Hold on.

1314
00:44:03,643 --> 00:44:05,483
Congratulations.

1315
00:44:05,483 --> 00:44:06,913
- Woo Jae...
- Thank you.

1316
00:44:06,913 --> 00:44:08,623
Woo Jae is soaked in sweat.

1317
00:44:09,353 --> 00:44:11,093
He's soaked in sweat.

1318
00:44:11,093 --> 00:44:12,093
(Done with this year's cardio)

1319
00:44:16,593 --> 00:44:18,963
With that, our guests...

1320
00:44:19,293 --> 00:44:22,733
get all the presents up to Round Three.

1321
00:44:23,363 --> 00:44:24,433
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

1322
00:44:24,433 --> 00:44:25,873
(Gifting a coffee machine, air purifier, and portable TV)

1323
00:44:25,873 --> 00:44:27,743
- What is it, Woo Jae?
- I'm worried.

1324
00:44:28,173 --> 00:44:29,473
I've grown attached to them.

1325
00:44:30,043 --> 00:44:31,473
But I won't see them next week.

1326
00:44:32,313 --> 00:44:34,143
We've grown so close to each other.

1327
00:44:34,543 --> 00:44:36,913
- Already?
- There's a sense of camaraderie.

1328
00:44:36,913 --> 00:44:38,353
- We do feel a sense of camaraderie.
- Yes.

1329
00:44:38,353 --> 00:44:41,083
- We do.
- By the way, John was very calm.

1330
00:44:41,153 --> 00:44:43,023
- Gosh. Good job, everyone.
- What a start.

1331
00:44:43,023 --> 00:44:44,123
- He was great.
- Yes.

1332
00:44:44,293 --> 00:44:45,423
Once again, Bit Na,

1333
00:44:45,423 --> 00:44:47,993
- congratulations to both of you.
- Thank you.

1334
00:44:47,993 --> 00:44:49,693
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1335
00:44:49,693 --> 00:44:52,863
Okay. How are you spending your precious spare time?

1336
00:44:52,863 --> 00:44:55,063
Whenever Possible Season 5, a natural dose of dopamine.

1337
00:44:55,263 --> 00:44:57,103
Join them at 5pm on Tuesdays.

1338
00:44:57,103 --> 00:44:58,273
It will begin now!

1339
00:44:58,273 --> 00:45:00,503
- Whenever Possible.
- Call us now.

1340
00:45:00,503 --> 00:45:01,943
(Send your letter to Whenever Possible now!)

1341
00:45:02,143 --> 00:45:03,543
We're off to a great start today.

1342
00:45:03,943 --> 00:45:05,443
- We had a great start.
- We'll enjoy lunch comfortably.

1343
00:45:05,943 --> 00:45:07,383
- That's right.
- Great spots are around here.

1344
00:45:07,383 --> 00:45:08,443
Right.

1345
00:45:08,613 --> 00:45:10,853
That's right, Woo Jae. Throughout your life,

1346
00:45:11,213 --> 00:45:12,753
- you need to stay humble.
- Exactly.

1347
00:45:13,183 --> 00:45:15,523
Keep that in mind. Okay?

1348
00:45:15,823 --> 00:45:17,693
The dopamine hits hard, right?

1349
00:45:17,693 --> 00:45:20,723
Yes. You don't need to watch shorts.

1350
00:45:20,893 --> 00:45:23,123
- Instead of watching shorts, - That's right.

1351
00:45:23,123 --> 00:45:25,433
- gather around and play this game.
- You're right.

1352
00:45:26,293 --> 00:45:29,133
- Anyway, we'll start again at 2pm.
- Shall we?

1353
00:45:29,133 --> 00:45:31,633
- We have an hour and a half.
- I'm feeling great so far.

1354
00:45:31,933 --> 00:45:33,903
- Let's enjoy our success and eat.
- Yes.

1355
00:45:33,903 --> 00:45:34,973
- Sounds good.
- Let's eat first and go.

1356
00:45:34,973 --> 00:45:36,103
- Of course.
- Yes.

1357
00:45:36,773 --> 00:45:37,973
What are we having?

1358
00:45:38,359 --> 00:45:39,919
- There are so many good options.
- Well.

1359
00:45:39,919 --> 00:45:41,929
How about pizza or burgers?

1360
00:45:41,929 --> 00:45:43,329
- Pizza?
- Should we go for Western food?

1361
00:45:43,329 --> 00:45:44,729
- Western food?
- Western food.

1362
00:45:44,899 --> 00:45:46,829
Western food sounds good once in a while.

1363
00:45:47,669 --> 00:45:50,969
- There's a really good pizza spot.
- Do you know the place?

1364
00:45:50,969 --> 00:45:52,499
- This one.
- Yes. I found that one too.

1365
00:45:52,869 --> 00:45:54,409
Should we go there? It's right next to us.

1366
00:45:54,409 --> 00:45:56,309
- It's right nearby.
- Yes. Let's go there.

1367
00:45:56,309 --> 00:45:57,539
- What do they have?
- Pizza.

1368
00:45:57,539 --> 00:45:59,079
- There's a great pizza spot.
- Sounds great.

1369
00:45:59,079 --> 00:46:01,179
- They sell Neapolitan pizza.
- I love it.

1370
00:46:01,779 --> 00:46:03,379
But there might be a queue.

1371
00:46:03,509 --> 00:46:05,619
- It's right nearby.
- Let's go and check.

1372
00:46:06,879 --> 00:46:08,049
We'll turn left now.

1373
00:46:09,389 --> 00:46:11,219
What? I don't see a queue.

1374
00:46:11,489 --> 00:46:12,719
- No?
- No.

1375
00:46:12,859 --> 00:46:13,989
What? Are they closed?

1376
00:46:14,189 --> 00:46:15,289
Are they closed?

1377
00:46:15,929 --> 00:46:17,729
Gosh. They open for lunch only on weekends.

1378
00:46:18,299 --> 00:46:19,859
They don't do lunch.

1379
00:46:20,129 --> 00:46:21,299
No wonder there was no queue.

1380
00:46:21,299 --> 00:46:22,929
Gosh. Pasta sounds good for the first time in a while.

1381
00:46:22,999 --> 00:46:24,399
Wait. I had pasta yesterday.

1382
00:46:24,399 --> 00:46:25,699
(They linger sadly in front of the restaurant.)

1383
00:46:26,439 --> 00:46:28,239
- What? It's raining.
- It's raining.

1384
00:46:29,539 --> 00:46:31,309
What did they have? Should I ask them?

1385
00:46:31,309 --> 00:46:32,479
Did you just eat?

1386
00:46:33,079 --> 00:46:34,209
- Yes.
- What did you have?

1387
00:46:34,379 --> 00:46:35,449
- We ate at our company cafeteria.
- At our cafeteria.

1388
00:46:35,579 --> 00:46:36,679
Your company cafeteria?

1389
00:46:36,779 --> 00:46:37,849
Their company cafeteria.

1390
00:46:38,449 --> 00:46:39,519
How's your company cafeteria?

1391
00:46:40,079 --> 00:46:42,019
- Why do you ask?
- Are you going to go there?

1392
00:46:42,289 --> 00:46:44,519
- He's a big fan of cafeterias.
- At your company? I see.

1393
00:46:45,189 --> 00:46:46,419
- Bye.
- Yes.

1394
00:46:46,419 --> 00:46:48,059
- Good luck.
- Let me search.

1395
00:46:48,729 --> 00:46:50,799
I don't need to search because they're all searching.

1396
00:46:50,859 --> 00:46:53,159
(The three younger ones start looking up restaurants.)

1397
00:46:53,359 --> 00:46:55,299
There's a great pork cutlet spot.

1398
00:46:55,299 --> 00:46:58,639
But I think there will be a line.

1399
00:46:59,069 --> 00:47:00,169
Wait. This is...

1400
00:47:00,569 --> 00:47:01,669
There's a barbecue place too.

1401
00:47:02,069 --> 00:47:04,179
I do like grilled meat,

1402
00:47:04,579 --> 00:47:06,909
but the smell will cling to us as it's raining.

1403
00:47:07,549 --> 00:47:08,709
Teppanyaki.

1404
00:47:09,849 --> 00:47:11,819
Teppanyaki doesn't sound good when it's raining.

1405
00:47:11,949 --> 00:47:14,249
Jae Seok is a type when asked what to have...

1406
00:47:14,249 --> 00:47:16,149
Didn't he step back,

1407
00:47:16,149 --> 00:47:18,919
- saying we were doing the search?
- Actually,

1408
00:47:18,919 --> 00:47:20,959
barbecuing is the only thing I'm reluctant about.

1409
00:47:20,959 --> 00:47:23,129
- We'll visit our next guest too.
- Right.

1410
00:47:23,589 --> 00:47:24,959
The tension will drop...

1411
00:47:25,199 --> 00:47:26,299
when we smell like barbecue.

1412
00:47:26,299 --> 00:47:27,969
- Is that so?
- Yes. A bit.

1413
00:47:28,329 --> 00:47:29,399
Western food, then?

1414
00:47:30,129 --> 00:47:32,139
- Anything's fine.
- Right up there,

1415
00:47:32,399 --> 00:47:34,339
- there's Kitchen 485.
- Sounds good.

1416
00:47:35,669 --> 00:47:36,809
(He's on board right away after hearing the name.)

1417
00:47:36,809 --> 00:47:38,479
Have I already told you about their menus?

1418
00:47:38,479 --> 00:47:40,409
What? I thought we were going there.

1419
00:47:40,509 --> 00:47:43,479
- They have lasagna, burrata...
- Great.

1420
00:47:43,479 --> 00:47:45,879
- They have oil-based pastas.
- Sounds great.

1421
00:47:46,279 --> 00:47:49,719
I think it'll cost about 200 dollars if we eat there.

1422
00:47:49,719 --> 00:47:50,989
- Sounds good.
- Is it an expensive spot?

1423
00:47:50,989 --> 00:47:52,959
- It's a bit costly.
- Let's go.

1424
00:47:52,959 --> 00:47:54,859
- Do you not feel confident?
- I'm fine.

1425
00:47:54,859 --> 00:47:56,959
- If you're scared, back out.
- I want to have expensive dishes.

1426
00:47:56,959 --> 00:47:59,859
- If you're scared, go somewhere...
- I love spending my money on shows.

1427
00:48:00,199 --> 00:48:01,399
- Let's go, then.
- Okay.

1428
00:48:01,399 --> 00:48:02,429
Let's go.

1429
00:48:02,429 --> 00:48:03,529
(They leave, acting tough.)

1430
00:48:04,139 --> 00:48:05,699
Gosh. Their wood-fired pizza looks good.

1431
00:48:05,699 --> 00:48:07,909
(Staring)

1432
00:48:08,609 --> 00:48:10,539
There was a cafe near here.

1433
00:48:11,179 --> 00:48:14,409
It was mentioned in one of 10cm's songs.

1434
00:48:14,409 --> 00:48:15,879
That cafe was right here.

1435
00:48:15,879 --> 00:48:18,419
I'm sorry, but I shot "Infinite Challenge" there.

1436
00:48:19,749 --> 00:48:21,749
Do I really have to mention that?

1437
00:48:21,749 --> 00:48:24,289
- I'll try many times today.
- Sure.

1438
00:48:24,589 --> 00:48:26,619
I shot "Infinite Challenge" there...

1439
00:48:26,619 --> 00:48:28,089
when 10cm came to the show.

1440
00:48:28,589 --> 00:48:29,859
(Sighing)

1441
00:48:29,859 --> 00:48:31,799
- It's an Italian restaurant.
- Italian.

1442
00:48:31,799 --> 00:48:32,859
It's right here.

1443
00:48:32,999 --> 00:48:34,729
- They make the pasta from scratch.
- Good.

1444
00:48:34,729 --> 00:48:37,069
- It's pretty.
- And there's no one here.

1445
00:48:37,069 --> 00:48:38,299
- Yes.
- Good.

1446
00:48:38,599 --> 00:48:39,669
Hello.

1447
00:48:39,969 --> 00:48:41,639
Where's the menu? It's this one.

1448
00:48:41,639 --> 00:48:42,969
We need to scan the QR code.

1449
00:48:43,509 --> 00:48:44,839
- Do we scan the QR code?
- Yes.

1450
00:48:44,839 --> 00:48:47,279
(Scanning the menu)

1451
00:48:47,279 --> 00:48:49,149
Gosh. This meal will cost us a bit.

1452
00:48:49,149 --> 00:48:50,879
- What? Wait.
- If you're scared...

1453
00:48:50,879 --> 00:48:53,049
- There's tenderloin steak.
- Are we having some steak?

1454
00:48:53,049 --> 00:48:54,619
- But...
- If you want to.

1455
00:48:54,619 --> 00:48:55,689
We should at least order one.

1456
00:48:55,689 --> 00:48:57,119
- We should order one.
- If you want to.

1457
00:48:57,119 --> 00:48:59,489
- Let's get a pizza.
- And a steak.

1458
00:48:59,689 --> 00:49:02,029
- And a risotto and two pastas.
- Sounds great.

1459
00:49:02,029 --> 00:49:04,089
I'll place our order here. I'll do it.

1460
00:49:04,089 --> 00:49:05,129
(Ordering a feast)

1461
00:49:05,799 --> 00:49:07,599
(Thinking)

1462
00:49:07,599 --> 00:49:10,199
I realized I like Yeon Seok...

1463
00:49:10,199 --> 00:49:11,939
- more than I thought.
- Why do you say that?

1464
00:49:12,699 --> 00:49:13,839
Come to think of it,

1465
00:49:13,839 --> 00:49:15,769
my all-time favorite music video is "Three of Us."

1466
00:49:17,239 --> 00:49:18,279
Considering that...

1467
00:49:18,279 --> 00:49:19,839
I co-starred in it with Gong Myoung.

1468
00:49:20,879 --> 00:49:22,079
Were you the bad guy again?

1469
00:49:22,379 --> 00:49:24,149
- No. He loses the girl.
- He loses her.

1470
00:49:24,149 --> 00:49:27,219
I have a crush on this girl, but my friend wins her over.

1471
00:49:27,219 --> 00:49:28,619
They get married.

1472
00:49:28,619 --> 00:49:30,449
And I play the piano at the wedding.

1473
00:49:31,189 --> 00:49:32,519
What a nice guy.

1474
00:49:32,519 --> 00:49:33,719
(Yeon Seok, the nice guy, 12 years ago)

1475
00:49:34,089 --> 00:49:36,029
You watched lots of my work.

1476
00:49:36,029 --> 00:49:38,329
I know. I just realized that too.

1477
00:49:38,559 --> 00:49:40,599
Recently, people around me have been saying...

1478
00:49:41,499 --> 00:49:43,629
that they love Woo Jae.

1479
00:49:43,629 --> 00:49:45,869
So many of my friends said so.

1480
00:49:46,039 --> 00:49:47,539
- Right.
- Then...

1481
00:49:48,009 --> 00:49:49,109
Tell them.

1482
00:49:49,939 --> 00:49:51,309
- So I...
- Tell them what?

1483
00:49:51,309 --> 00:49:52,939
What? To take a good look at him again.

1484
00:49:54,039 --> 00:49:55,109
He's driving me nuts.

1485
00:49:55,109 --> 00:49:56,279
They find him so funny.

1486
00:49:56,279 --> 00:49:58,449
He's funny while being so stylish at the same time.

1487
00:49:58,449 --> 00:49:59,919
He has the body for variety shows.

1488
00:50:00,349 --> 00:50:01,389
He's born with it.

1489
00:50:01,389 --> 00:50:02,849
When I saw him play the game just now,

1490
00:50:03,389 --> 00:50:05,359
I thought he was good in the beginning.

1491
00:50:05,359 --> 00:50:07,789
He was really good in the beginning,

1492
00:50:07,929 --> 00:50:10,029
but like you said, Jae Seok,

1493
00:50:10,029 --> 00:50:11,959
- he wasn't persistent.
- You're right.

1494
00:50:11,959 --> 00:50:13,699
- He can't keep up for long.
- He lacks endurance.

1495
00:50:13,699 --> 00:50:14,869
- He lacks stamina.
- Yes.

1496
00:50:14,869 --> 00:50:17,799
Mentally, I can't keep up for long.

1497
00:50:18,539 --> 00:50:19,639
Right. You collapse.

1498
00:50:19,639 --> 00:50:21,869
Still, we did a great job.

1499
00:50:21,869 --> 00:50:23,009
It was really...

1500
00:50:23,009 --> 00:50:24,309
That was really intense.

1501
00:50:24,779 --> 00:50:28,549
- Park maintained his pace.
- He was really good.

1502
00:50:28,749 --> 00:50:29,779
You were reliable.

1503
00:50:29,779 --> 00:50:31,849
- Thank you.
- Going first wasn't easy.

1504
00:50:31,849 --> 00:50:33,919
- He's very calm.
- Yes.

1505
00:50:34,249 --> 00:50:35,949
That plays a big role in a game like this.

1506
00:50:36,649 --> 00:50:37,859
I get worked up easily.

1507
00:50:38,159 --> 00:50:40,559
- Did you just yawn?
- Yes. I was bored.

1508
00:50:42,229 --> 00:50:43,759
Did you yawn when I was talking?

1509
00:50:44,659 --> 00:50:46,099
